b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/"},{"text":"beginners","kind":"document","id":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438:p34","snapshotId":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/"},{"text":"who are new to programming.","kind":"document","id":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438:p35","snapshotId":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/"},{"text":"Python is an easy to learn, powerful programming language. It has efficient\nhigh-level data structures and a simple but effective approach to\nobject-oriented programming. Python’s elegant syntax and dynamic typing,\ntogether with its interpreted nature, make it an ideal language for scripting\nand rapid application development in many areas on most platforms.","kind":"document","id":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438:p36","snapshotId":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/"},{"text":"The Python interpreter and the extensive standard library are freely available\nin source or binary form for all major platforms from the Python website,","kind":"document","id":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438:p37","snapshotId":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/"},{"text":"https://www.python.org/","kind":"document","id":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438:p38","snapshotId":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/"},{"text":", and may be freely distributed. The same site also\ncontains distributions of and pointers to many free third party Python modules,\nprograms and tools, and additional documentation.","kind":"document","id":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438:p39","snapshotId":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/"},{"text":"The Python interpreter is easily extended with new functions and data types\nimplemented in C or C++ (or other languages callable from C). Python is also\nsuitable as an extension language for customizable applications.","kind":"document","id":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438:p40","snapshotId":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/"},{"text":"This tutorial introduces the reader informally to the basic concepts and\nfeatures of the Python language and system. Be aware that it expects you to\nhave a basic understanding of programming in general. It helps to have a Python\ninterpreter handy for hands-on experience, but all examples are self-contained,\nso the tutorial can be read off-line as well.","kind":"document","id":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438:p41","snapshotId":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/"}],"omittedPassages":false,"interactiveElements":[],"accessibilityTreeSummary":"Read-only source; no offered actions.","timestamp":"2026-10-18T11:31:50.441Z"}}
{"version":1,"timestamp":"2026-10-18T11:31:50.445Z","runId":"run_mvdqwioo_76x17en","type":"observation","payload":{"snapshotId":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438","documentId":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/","title":"docs.python.org","visibleText":"Theme\nPrevious topic\nChangelog\nNext topic\n1.\nWhetting Your Appetite\nThis page\nReport a bug\nImprove this page\nShow source\nNavigation\nindex\nmodules\n|\nnext\n|\nprevious\n|\nPython\n»\n3.15.0 Documentation\n»\nThe Python Tutorial\n|\nTheme\n|\nThe Python Tutorial\n¶\nTip\nThis tutorial is designed for\nprogrammers\nthat are new to the Python language,\nnot\nbeginners\nwho are new to programming.\nPython is an easy to learn, powerful programming language. It has efficient\nhigh-level data structures and a simple but effective approach to\nobject-oriented programming. Python’s elegant syntax and dynamic typing,\ntogether with its interpreted nature, make it an ideal language for scripting\nand rapid application development in many areas on most platforms.\nThe Python interpreter and the extensive standard library are freely available\nin source or binary form for all major platforms from the Python website,\nhttps://www.python.org/\n, and may be freely distributed. The same site also\ncontains distributions of and pointers to many free third party Python modules,\nprograms and tools, and additional documentation.\nThe Python interpreter is easily extended with new functions and data types\nimplemented in C or C++ (or other languages callable from C). Python is also\nsuitable as an extension language for customizable applications.\nThis tutorial introduces the reader informally to the basic concepts and\nfeatures of the Python language and system. Be aware that it expects you to\nhave a basic understanding of programming in general. It helps to have a Python\ninterpreter handy for hands-on experience, but all examples are self-contained,\nso the tutorial can be read off-line as well.","passages":[{"text":"Theme","kind":"document","id":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438:p1","snapshotId":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/"},{"text":"Previous topic","kind":"document","id":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438:p2","snapshotId":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/"},{"text":"Changelog","kind":"document","id":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438:p3","snapshotId":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/"},{"text":"Next topic","kind":"document","id":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438:p4","snapshotId":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/"},{"text":"1.","kind":"document","id":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438:p5","snapshotId":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/"},{"text":"Whetting Your Appetite","kind":"document","id":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438:p6","snapshotId":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/"},{"text":"This page","kind":"document","id":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438:p7","snapshotId":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/"},{"text":"Report a bug","kind":"document","id":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438:p8","snapshotId":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/"},{"text":"Improve this page","kind":"document","id":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438:p9","snapshotId":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/"},{"text":"Show source","kind":"document","id":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438:p10","snapshotId":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/"},{"text":"Navigation","kind":"document","id":"234b42d5-b346-4409-97a6-eb2f794b3438:p11","snapshotId":"234b42d5-b346-4409-9